      "payload": {
        "fork": "guard mechanism (revised in round 1)",
        "choice": "Replaced the Bun.main keying with one Bun.plugin per Vitest-owned package whose onLoad filter is scoped to that package directory. Round-1 lens.adversarial-testing proved P0 AT-1: a preload evaluates once per process and Bun.main names only the first test file, so a bare or multi-target bun test still walked into the frontend files. onLoad fires per test file, so every target is classified. onResolve was ruled out empirically (it does not fire for entry-point test files), and the filter is scoped so the handler always exits and never needs the pass-through return Bun requires."
      }
